# RUN: llc --mtriple=aie2 -O2 --start-before=postmisched %s -o - | FileCheck %s
# RUN: llc --mtriple=aie2 -O2 --start-before=postmisched \
# RUN:     --aie-interblock-loop-exit-depth=false %s -o - | \
# RUN:     FileCheck --check-prefix=NOEXIT %s

# The preheader ends with a VMAC whose accumulator is only consumed after the
# loop. The loop body runs at least MinTripCount - 1 times, so the VMAC doesn't
# need to complete when the loop is entered. With a minimum trip count of 5 it
# is scheduled closer to the loop; with a minimum trip count of 2 the loop is
# only guaranteed to run once and the schedule doesn't change.
#
# deadOnSkipPath has no loop. bb.0 ends with a VMAC whose accumulator is only
# read in bb.3, deep enough not to constrain it. The fallthrough bb.1 is a
# single bundle in which cm0 is dead. bb.0 keeps three empty bundles after the
# VMAC. Even if the ExitSU edge of bb.0 -> bb.1 ignored the dead cm0, the
# interblock scoreboard blocks every cycle after bb.1, and the VMAC writes cm0
# through CM_WA_PORT four cycles after issue.
# liveOnSkipPath is the control: bb.2 reads cm0, so the same three bundles are
# required there.

--- |
